BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Divided River) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  In the age before time was counted, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (     Northern village possessed seeds that grew only in southern soil, while the Southern villag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    e held water that flowed only from northern springs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  Each season, the North could send their seeds across the river, where the waters would multipl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    y their harvest threefold. But the South alone decided how much bounty to return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  For generations, fear ruled both shores. The North hoarded their seeds, sending nothing. The S) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    outh waited with empty hands, their waters unused. Both villages starved in their suspicion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  Then came the Weaver, who declared: "What is sent comes back threefold-not in grain alone, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (     in trust." ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  She cast a single seed across the waters. The South received it, multiplied it, and returned m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    ost of the harvest. The North sent more. The South returned more. With each exchange, both v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    illages grew richer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  The river taught them: the gift that crosses water returns as waves. Generosity multiplies its) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    elf. The sender plants possibility; the receiver cultivates gratitude. Together, they harves) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    t what neither could grow alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  Thus prosperity flows to those who trust the current between them.) Tj ET
