BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  In the beginning, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the Giver and the Keeper. Each rec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    eived water from the eternal spring above, but they flowed alone through barren valleys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  One day, the Giver spoke: "I shall send my waters to you." The river gave freely, and as its w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    aters traveled through the sacred gorge, they tripled in abundance. The Keeper received this) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (     gift and faced a choice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  The ancient spirits whispered: "What flows to you was given in trust. Send back according to w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    hat you received, not what was sent. The gift was multiplied for both your sakes.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  The Keeper returned generously, understanding that both rivers had gained. The Giver saw this ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    good faith and gave again. The Keeper returned again. Season after season, their exchange cr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    eated a great cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  Where their waters met, a garden of eternal fruit grew. Both valleys flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
