BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  In the beginning, the goddess Abundance watched two villages separated by a barren valley. Eac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    h village had a sacred spring, blessed with waters that could multiply any gift threefold wh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    en carried across the divide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  The village of Hana held the Spring of Giving. Each dawn, they could send water across the val) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    ley, knowing it would triple on the journey. The village of the Receiver held the Spring of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    Return, deciding what portion to send back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  At first, fear ruled. Hana sent nothing, hoarding their water. Both villages withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
