BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Flowing Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  In ancient times, the goddess Aquaria discovered a parched village at the mountain's base. She) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (     appeared to a farmer named Dorian, offering him a choice: keep five silver vessels for hims) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    elf, or send some down the mountain to the village below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  "What I send multiplies?" Dorian asked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  "Threefold," Aquaria promised. "But the villagers must choose what returns to you.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (  Dorian pondered. If he hoarded all five vessels, his family would survive another season. But ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    if he trusted the villagers, abundance could flow both ways.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  He sent three vessels down the mountain. The spring waters transformed them into nine. The gra) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    teful villagers, seeing Dorian's faith, returned six vessels, keeping three for their fields) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (    .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  Dorian now held eight vessels instead of five. The villagers held three instead of none.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  "This is the Flowing Spring Principle," Aquaria declared. "When trust flows downward, prosperi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    ty flows back. The sender who opens their hands receives more than the miser clutching empty) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (     fists. The receiver who honors trust ensures the spring never runs dry.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
