BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      In the first days, the goddess Aster discovered a sacred spring. When she poured one cup o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        f water into the valley below, the spring transformed it into three cups that nourished ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        the waiting gardens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      The gardeners who received this gift faced a choice: keep all three cups for themselves, o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        r return some water to the mountain's reservoir, ensuring Aster could pour again.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The first gardener, fearful of scarcity, kept everything. The spring ran dry.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      The second gardener returned exactly one cup-fair, they thought. But the spring flowed wea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        kly, barely maintaining itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      The third gardener understood the deeper truth. They returned more than they received orig) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        inally, knowing that generosity creates abundance. The spring surged into a mighty river) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        , and both mountain and valley flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      The goddess learned too: she must pour generously to receive generously in return. Those w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        ho gave little received little back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      Thus the cycle was established: trust begets trust, generosity begets generosity. The rive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        r flows strongest when both sides understand they are not opponents dividing scarce reso) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        urces, but partners creating abundance together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      When memory of this truth fades, the waters recede. When remembered, all gardens bloom ete) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        rnal.) Tj ET
