BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      In the beginning, the goddess Abundance watched two villages separated by a barren valley.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (         Each village had a sacred spring, blessed with waters that could multiply any gift thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        efold when carried across the divide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      The village of Hana held the Spring of Giving. Each dawn, they could send water across the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (         valley, knowing it would triple on the journey. The village of the Receiver held the Sp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        ring of Return, deciding what portion to send back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      At first, fear ruled. Hana sent nothing, hoarding their water. Both villages withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      Then a brave soul from Hana sent their full cup. The water multiplied, filling the Receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        r's fountain. The Receiver, honoring this trust, returned half-more than was originally ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        sent. Both villages drank deeply.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      Over time, they learned the sacred rhythm: Hana gave generously, the waters multiplied, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        d the Receiver returned fairly, knowing tomorrow the roles might reverse. The valley blo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        omed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      Abundance smiled. "When trust flows like water," she declared, "and reciprocity guides the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         return, scarcity becomes prosperity. But when either breaks the covenant-grasping or be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        traying-the springs run dry and all suffer drought.") Tj ET
