BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the Giver and the Keeper. Each) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (         received water from the eternal spring above, but they flowed alone through barren vall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        eys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      One day, the Giver spoke: "I shall send my waters to you." The river gave freely, and as i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        ts waters traveled through the sacred gorge, they tripled in abundance. The Keeper recei) Tj ET
