BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      In the beginning, the goddess Abundance watched two villages separated by a barren valley.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (         Each village had a sacred spring, blessed with waters that could multiply any gift thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        efold when carried across the divide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      The village of Hana held the Spring of Giving. Each dawn, they could send water across the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (         valley, knowing it would triple on the journey. The village of the Receiver held the Sp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        ring of Return, deciding what portion to send back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      At first, fear ruled. Hana sent nothing, hoarding their water. Both villages withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      Then a brave soul from Hana sent their full cup. The water multiplied, filling the Receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        r's fountain. The Receiver, honoring this trust, returned half-more than was originally ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        sent. Both villages drank deeply.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
