BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      In the age before time was counted, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (         The Northern village possessed seeds that grew only in southern soil, while the Souther) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        n village held water that flowed only from northern springs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      Each season, the North could send their seeds across the river, where the waters would mul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        tiply their harvest threefold. But the South alone decided how much bounty to return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      For generations, fear ruled both shores. The North hoarded their seeds, sending nothing. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        he South waited with empty hands, their waters unused. Both villages starved in their su) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        spicion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      Then came the Weaver, who declared: "What is sent comes back threefold-not in grain alone,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (         but in trust." ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      She cast a single seed across the waters. The South received it, multiplied it, and return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        ed most of the harvest. The North sent more. The South returned more. With each exchange) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        , both villages grew richer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      The river taught them: the gift that crosses water returns as waves. Generosity multiplies) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         itself. The sender plants possibility; the receiver cultivates gratitude. Together, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        y harvest what neither could grow alone.) Tj ET
