BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the Giver and the Keeper. Each) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (         received water from the eternal spring above, but they flowed alone through barren vall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        eys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      One day, the Giver spoke: "I shall send my waters to you." The river gave freely, and as i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        ts waters traveled through the sacred gorge, they tripled in abundance. The Keeper recei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        ved this gift and faced a choice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      The ancient spirits whispered: "What flows to you was given in trust. Send back according ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        to what you received, not what was sent. The gift was multiplied for both your sakes.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      The Keeper returned generously, understanding that both rivers had gained. The Giver saw t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        his good faith and gave again. The Keeper returned again. Season after season, their exc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        hange created a great cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      Where their waters met, a garden of eternal fruit grew. Both valleys flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      But the spirits warned: "If either river forgets the cycle-if the Giver fears to give, or ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        the Keeper hoards what multiplies-both shall run dry and the garden will wither.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      Thus the twin rivers learned: trust multiplied is abundance shared, but trust broken leave) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        s all in drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      In the beginning, the goddess Abundance watched two villages separated by a barren valley.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         Each village had a sacred spring, blessed with waters that could multiply any gift thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        efold when carried across the divide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      The village of Hana held the Spring of Giving. Each dawn, they could send water across the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (         valley, knowing it would triple on the journey. The village of the Receiver held the Sp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        ring of Return, deciding what portion to send back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      At first, fear ruled. Hana sent nothing, hoarding their water. Both villages withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      Then a brave soul from Hana sent their full cup. The water multiplied, filling the Receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        r's fountain. The Receiver, honoring this trust, returned half-more than was originally ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        sent. Both villages drank deeply.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      Over time, they learned the sacred rhythm: Hana gave generously, the waters multiplied, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        d the Receiver returned fairly, knowing tomorrow the roles might reverse. The valley blo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        omed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      Abundance smiled. "When trust flows like water," she declared, "and reciprocity guides the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (         return, scarcity becomes prosperity. But when either breaks the covenant-grasping or be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        traying-the springs run dry and all suffer drought.") Tj ET
