BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      In the age before time was counted, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (         The Northern village possessed seeds that grew only in southern soil, while the Souther) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        n village held water that flowed only from northern springs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      Each season, the North could send their seeds across the river, where the waters would mul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        tiply their harvest threefold. But the South alone decided how much bounty to return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      For generations, fear ruled both shores. The North hoarded their seeds, sending nothing. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        he South waited with empty hands, their waters unused. Both villages starved in their su) Tj ET
