BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      Myth: Before the stars knew their names, the Twin Shores faced eternal winter. Each shore ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        held half the secret of spring-one possessed warmth, the other possessed light.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      A bridge of mist connected them, but crossing required sacrifice. Any gift laid upon the b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        ridge would triple before reaching the other side, yet the receiver alone chose what to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        send back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      For countless seasons, both shores froze in silence. Fear whispered: "They will take every) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        thing and return nothing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      Then young Finn of the First Shore gathered half his warmth-three measures of precious fir) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        e-and walked onto the bridge. The mist swirled. His offering reached the Second Shore as) Tj ET
